707:   /**
708:    * Command to pin the Zeebe engine's internal clock to a specific time.
709:    *
710:    * <p>This method initiates a command to pin the clock to a specified time. You can specify the
711:    * time using either an epoch timestamp in milliseconds or an {@link java.time.Instant} object.
712:    *
713:    * <p>Once pinned, the clock will remain at the specified time and will not advance until another
714:    * <code>pin</code> or <code>reset</code> command is issued. This is useful for scenarios where
715:    * you need to simulate process execution at a specific point in time.
716:    *
717:    * <p>Example usage:
718:    *
719:    * <pre>{@code
720:    * final long pinnedTime = 1742461285000L; // Thu, Mar 20, 2025 09:01:25 GMT+0000
721:    * camundaClient
722:    *  .newClockPinCommand()
723:    *  .time(pinnedTime)
724:    *  .send();
725:    *
726:    * final Instant futureInstant = Instant.now().plus(Duration.ofDays(7));
727:    * camundaClient
728:    *  .newClockPinCommand()
729:    *  .time(futureInstant)
730:    *  .send();
731:    * }</pre>
732:    *
733:    * <p>The command is marked as <strong>experimental</strong> and may undergo changes or
