522:    * then publishes them to the client. The given worker is called for every received job, works on
523:    * them and eventually completes them.
524:    *
525:    * <pre>
526:    * JobWorker worker = camundaClient
527:    *  .newWorker()
528:    *  .jobType("payment")
529:    *  .handler(paymentHandler)
530:    *  .open();
531:    *
532:    * ...
533:    * worker.close();
534:    * </pre>
535:    *
536:    * Example JobHandler implementation:
537:    *
538:    * <pre>
539:    * public final class PaymentHandler implements JobHandler
540:    * {
541:    *   &#64;Override
542:    *   public void handle(JobClient client, JobEvent jobEvent)
543:    *   {
544:    *     String json = jobEvent.getVariables();
545:    *     // modify variables
546:    *
547:    *     client
548:    *      .newCompleteCommand()
549:    *      .event(jobEvent)
550:    *      .variables(json)
551:    *      .send();
552:    *   }
553:    * };
554:    * </pre>
555:    *
556:    * @return a builder for the worker registration
557:    */
